implementationPlan.description:
Write the regression test first: create packages/moe-daemon/src/tools/parkedReview.guard.test.ts with your own editor (Write on Claude, apply_patch on codex exec), never a shell copy, because the TOOL witness matters at landing. Start from the architect's prototype at /mnt/d/moe-scratch/plan-e44fbbf3/parkedReview.guard.test.ts (151 lines). Against the unfixed sources at f76c55f3 it gives 4 failed / 2 passed; with the fix all 6 pass.

The test parks task-1 through the real hard-cap path: a 4th qa_reject by qa-a at reopenCount 3. qa-b is a QA seat busy on its own task-2. It then pins:
(a) it.each over qa-b and a governor-x seat:
  - qa_approve and qa_reject called with that workerId reject with code NOT_ALLOWED (-32003), codeName 'NOT_ALLOWED', and a message containing 'parked for human review';
  - the task file is byte-identical;
  - status is REVIEW, assignedWorkerId null, reopenCount 4, needsHumanReview true, rejectionHistory length 1;
  - qa-b stays CODING on task-2, so no touchWorker runs on a refused caller.
(b) release_task with workerId worker-x and a valid handoffNote is refused NOT_ALLOWED; the row stays parked and the file stays byte-identical (no handoff persisted).
(c) get_context by qa-b returns no moe.qa_approve nextAction.
(d) Controls:
  - a workerId-less release_task unparks (needsHumanReview false);
  - a workerId-less qa_approve lands DONE and clears the flag;
  - an UNPARKED unassigned REVIEW row keeps the legacy seat path (the get_context hint is qa_approve, and qa_approve by qa-b lands DONE).

Assert exact codes and field values, never truthiness, so the test is mutation-resistant. Error handling in the test: afterEach removes its temp dir, and the claim-fence contrast uses its own idle seat qa-c. qa-b holds task-2, so a claim by qa-b answers alreadyAssigned first.
